---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro'
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro'
import { SITE_PRODUCT } from '../lib/site'
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms — ${SITE_PRODUCT}`}
  description={`The terms that apply to the ${SITE_PRODUCT} website and to using the ${SITE_PRODUCT} desktop application, in plain language.`}
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These terms cover the {SITE_PRODUCT} website and your use of the {SITE_PRODUCT} desktop
        application. They are written to be read, not skimmed past.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="software">
      <p class="mono" id="software">01 · The software</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          {SITE_PRODUCT} is free, open-source desktop software published by Vyotiq. The license is
          the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later), as recorded in the
          repository's <code>package.json</code> and <code>LICENSE</code> file. You can read, modify,
          and redistribute the software under that license.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="license">
      <p class="mono" id="license">02 · The license governs the software</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The GPL is the agreement that governs the software itself. Nothing on this page changes,
          restricts, or replaces it. If anything here seemed to conflict with the GPL for your use of
          the software, the GPL would control.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="repositories">
      <p class="mono" id="repositories">03 · Your repositories are yours</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          You keep all rights to your code, your files, and your data. {SITE_PRODUCT} runs locally
          and works on the repositories you open; the app never claims a license over your content by
          virtue of editing it. What you do with your repositories, including committing or sharing
          the <code>.vyotiq</code> folder the app writes, stays your call.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="privacy">
      <p class="mono" id="privacy">04 · Privacy</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The <a class="text-link" href="/privacy">privacy page</a> lists what is stored and what
          leaves your machine, including the conditions under which error reports are sent. Those
          statements are part of these terms by reference.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="downloads">
      <p class="mono" id="downloads">05 · Downloads and updates</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Installers and updates are distributed through the project's GitHub Releases repository
          (<code>vyotiqai/vyotiq-agent-v-releases</code>). GitHub's own terms apply to your use of
          GitHub's service. The app checks that repository for new versions and never downloads one
          without your approval.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="website">
      <p class="mono" id="website">06 · The website</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The documentation, changelog, and other pages on vyotiq.com are provided as-is for
          information. We may add, change, or remove pages over time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="warranty">
      <p class="mono" id="warranty">07 · No warranty</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          As the GPL states, the program is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, unless
          required by applicable law. It may have defects, and you use it at your own risk. Keep
          backups and review changes the agent makes to your files.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="liability">
      <p class="mono" id="liability">08 · Limitation of liability</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          As the GPL states, and except when required by applicable law, neither the copyright holder
          nor contributors are liable to you for damages, including general, special, incidental, or
          consequential damages, arising out of the use of or inability to use the program. This
          section follows the license; it does not narrow any protection the GPL gives you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="use">
      <p class="mono" id="use">09 · Acceptable use</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Use the software and this site lawfully and respect other people's rights. Do not use the
          site to distribute malware, attack its availability, or misrepresent who published the
          software.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="changes">
      <p class="mono" id="changes">10 · Changes to these terms</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We may revise these terms as the product changes. The GPL license for the software itself
          can only change as the GPL allows. The date below shows when this page was last updated.
        </p>
        <p class="mono updated">Last updated: 2026-09-12</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="contact">
      <p class="mono" id="contact">11 · Contact</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Questions about these terms go to
          <a class="text-link" href="mailto:support@vyotiq.com">support@vyotiq.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding: var(--space-9, 96px) 0 var(--space-6, 32px);
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: var(--space-4, 16px) 0 var(--space-5, 24px);
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .block {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    padding: var(--space-6, 32px) 0;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .mono {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4, 16px);
  }

  .prose p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4, 16px);
  }

  .prose p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .prose code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.875em;
    background: var(--well);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.125em 0.375em;
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
